# All-Out Assault: "When this enchantment enters, if it's your main phase, there is an additional combat phase after this phase
# followed by an additional main phase. When you next attack this turn, untap each creature you control." (CR 500.8, 505.1, 603.7b).
# Cast in the precombat main on turn 3, it puts a combat and a main phase before the turn's own combat. Fanatical Firebrand (1/1 haste,
# +1/+1 from the enchantment) attacks in the additional combat, and the delayed ability untaps it as attackers are declared; it attacks
# again in the turn's own combat, which does not untap it a second time (the ability was "next"). Bot2 goes 20 -> 18 -> 16.

